  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/417983">Corollary <span data-tag="417983">4.4.5.7</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category. Then the restriction map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Fun (\Idem ^{+}, \calC ) \rightarrow \Fun (\Ret , \calC ) \]
</div>
  <p> from strong retraction diagrams to weak retraction diagrams is a trivial fibration of simplicial sets. In particular, every weak retraction diagram in $\calC $ can be extended to a strong retraction diagram. </p>
